# tally 2.1.7 S1 (#93, F11b; the plan's critic C-20): a walked value of a day before S is HOLE-PRERUN `before
# the run's start` (L §8.1), bal and low as flows already was; HOLE-ANCHOR is for a read inside the run before a
# place's first reading. Run 2026-02-01 .. 2026-03-31; a stated reading of konto at 2026-01-05 end and an opening at
# 2026-02-01 start: bal on 2026-01-20 (a), low over 2026-01-20 .. 2026-02-15 (b) and bal on the stated day (d) are
# the hole; bal inside the run reads the opening (c). Was (2.1.6): a, b, d "konto has no balance before
# 2026-01-05", a question false of the day read.
=== pre.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-02-01
  end 2026-03-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  anchor konto
  stated[konto] = 40.00 PLN at 2026-01-05 end "s"
  opening[konto] = 50.00 PLN at 2026-02-01 start "s"

ask a: bal(konto, 2026-01-20)
ask b: low(konto, 2026-01-20 .. 2026-02-15)
ask c: bal(konto, 2026-02-15)
ask d: bal(konto, 2026-01-05)
=== expect
a: ?"before the run's start" (konto)
  cut 2026-10-18
b: ?"before the run's start" (konto)
  cut 2026-10-18
c: 50.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-18
d: ?"before the run's start" (konto)
  cut 2026-10-18
